## Protocol boundary and next owner route

No registered path appends an audit result to an existing
`SESSION_PROTOKOLL`. `team-record` creates a new typed receipt
`docs/session_protocols/team-record-<event_id>.json`
(`docs/cartographer/TOOLS.yaml:968–975`; frozen runtime `:3061–3075`).
`close-session --protocol-out` uses atomic write
(`specs_docs/session_close.py:154–164,204–207`) and has no append mode; do
not pass the existing `SESSION_PROTOKOLL_2026-09-11_CODEX.md` as
`--protocol-out`. `--semantic-refresh` explicitly forbids `--protocol-out`
(`specs_docs/session_close.py:188–191`). This audit does not design a new
writer or modify the existing protocol.

The minimal owner route is: complete `team-integrate-candidate` with the
exact reviewed manifest and readback; confirm the relevant observation through
registered `resume-checkpoint` where required while preserving operation ID
and predecessor hash; run `plan`, then registered `close-session` for named
owned paths and derived-status verification; validate exact changed paths;
commit only owned candidate paths plus explicitly generated typed receipts;
pull with rebase and push the exact ordinary commit under the existing owner
grant. `workflow-session-close` is session closure, not Git delivery
(`docs/cartographer/TOOLS.yaml:1030–1042`).

Audit status: **SOURCE_INTEGRATION_APPROVED not observed; publication not
observed; owner action remains pending.**
